+bool ChFi3d_Builder::PerformCapAtMitre(const int theIndex)
+{
+  // The side iad of the fillet has left its face Fad across a
+  // sharp arc A at CP1 before the end of the surfdata Fprev, the
+  // side iop ends at its end on an arc C at CP2, where the path on
+  // the face Fv2 beyond was lost (a fillet of the same radius
+  // along C). The last surfdata Fd is computed on the extended
+  // surfaces of Fad and Fop. Fv1 beyond A and Fv2 meet at the
+  // vertex along an edge E, which the fillet crosses at M in Fd.
+  // The fillet is cut along Fv1 from CP1, across the section
+  // between Fprev and Fd (point X1), to M, and along Fv2 (a mitre)
+  // from CP2 to M. Fprev is split at CP1: its end part Fb takes Fv1
+  // on the side iad; Fd takes Fv1 and Fv2 and ends at M.
